{
  "slug": "repo-visuals",
  "name": "Repo Visuals",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "repo-visuals turns any open-source repo into a bespoke README hero — animated GIF or static PNG — through a structured discovery dialog. It scans the codebase, recommends a format that fits the repo's identity (terminal demo, product UI, brand wordmark, banner, diagram-as-hero), generates tailored HTML, previews it in your browser, and exports a retina-quality artifact ready to drop into the README.\n\nKey features:\n- Five-phase craft loop: discover → build → preview → export → output\n- Three operating modes (Auto / Semi-auto / Manual) that scale from \"decide nothing\" to \"decide everything\"\n- Format-aware: GIF for motion-worthy demos, PNG when stillness reads better, HTML when the README itself can host it\n- Retina capture via Puppeteer + ffmpeg; automatic file-size and dimension validation\n- Optional 4-rater scorecard (User / Claude / Code / AI-vision-blind) for measuring craft quality across runs\n- Optional upstream PR: detects ownership, forks if needed, opens a PR with alt-text included\n- Heroes already merged into HTMLHint, Terminal.Gui, ast-graph, and others",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 skills**, `repo-visuals` (Create hero visuals — animated GIF, static PNG, or animated SVG — for GitHub repositories), `repo-visuals-retro` (Retrospective meta-skill for the `repo-visuals` skill).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install repo-visuals@claude-community` from `livlign/claude-skills` (`plugins/repo-visuals`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
